WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.140
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:15.060
The reading from the Sinaxadion for October 1st, on which we commemorate St. Gregory,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:22.270
the Choirmaster, Domesticals of the Great Lavra.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:28.030
St. Gregory was a chanter at the Great Lavra on the Holy Mountain of Athos at the same time

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.910
as St. John Cucuceles.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:37.710
Once on the eve of the Theophany, God put into his heart during the Holy Liturgy to chant

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:45.510
the hymn, O full of grace, thou who art the joy of all creation.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.950
Instead of the accustomed, it is very meat to bless thee.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:57.750
Whereupon the Mother of God appeared to him, thanked him, and just as she had done for St. John

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:04.350
Cucuceles gave him a gold coin as a pledge of her favor.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:09.990
This coin has been kept ever since by the monks of the Lavra.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:17.990
Having led a life acceptable to God, St. Gregory fell asleep in peace.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:24.510
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.670
and save us.
